#reason src/cli/lantern Gives terminals a command that opens a folder in its own window, launching a new instance so the argument is not dropped.
#reason src/main/cli.ts Accepts --project only for an existing directory by its real path and never replaces a lantern command it did not install.
#reason src/main/windows.ts Holds the window registry so one window per real checkout is opened or focused and gets the project's provider.
#reason src/renderer/features/cli-panel.ts Shows the lantern command state in Settings and tells the user how to replace a foreign command by hand.
#reason src/shared/shell-quote.ts Single shell quoting helper shared by the main process and the settings panel.
#reason test/cli-panel.test.ts Covers every state of the command line panel including a foreign command.
#reason test/cli-script.test.ts Runs the real lantern script against a stub open for spaces, symlinks, the .app launch and the bundle id launch.
#reason test/cli.test.ts Covers --project validation and that install never overwrites a foreign command.
#reason test/project-window.test.ts Checks the toolbar keeps the map, Skills, microphone, mode switch and provider selector.
#reason test/windows.test.ts Covers the window lifecycle: dedupe by root, focus, removal on close, argv, pop-out and resize scoping.
#reason CONTRIBUTING.md Shows how to try a project window in development without installing the command.
#reason README.md Documents the lantern command, the project window toolbar and that a foreign command is never replaced.
#reason package.json Ships the cli folder as an extra resource so the packaged app carries the lantern command.
#reason scripts/esbuild.mjs Copies the lantern script into the build output and makes it executable.
#reason src/main/main.ts Delegates window handling to windows.ts, scopes cancel to the run's window and keeps a project window out of the saved list.
#reason src/main/popout.ts Remembers which window opened each pop-out so closing one window no longer closes another's.
#reason src/main/projectroot.ts Adds checkoutTop so a folder the user named keeps its own linked worktree as the window key.
#reason src/main/projects.ts Lists a project that has its own window only while that window is open, so it never lands in the saved sidebar list.
#reason src/preload/workspace.ts Exposes the command status and install calls to the settings panel.
#reason src/renderer/features/load-screen.ts Uses the shared el helper instead of a private copy.
#reason src/renderer/features/settings.ts Adds the Command line panel to the dialog and uses the shared el helper.
#reason src/renderer/global.d.ts Types the new command status and install bridge calls.
#reason src/renderer/lib/settings-editor.ts Lets the editor mount extra panels with their own table of contents entries.
#reason src/renderer/lib/settings-search.ts Makes panels searchable by their keywords next to ordinary settings.
#reason src/renderer/lib/util.ts Holds the one shared el helper and the macOS check.
#reason src/renderer/settings.css Styles the panel group and the command line panel.
#reason src/renderer/workspace.css Turns the sidebar into a compact toolbar in a project window and drags it only on macOS.
#reason src/renderer/workspace.html Names the microphone button so it stays labelled when the toolbar hides its text.
#reason src/renderer/workspace.ts Marks a project window, claims its project and wires its provider selector to that project.
#reason test/lantern-bundle.test.ts Checks every installOnOpen call site passes the project provider instead of counting calls.
#reason test/projectroot.test.ts Covers checkoutTop for plain folders, subfolders and linked worktrees.
#reason test/projects.test.ts Checks a windowed project is listed only while open and never saved.
#reason test/settings-dialog.test.ts Checks the Command line entry opens its panel in the Settings dialog.
#reason test/settings-editor.test.ts Covers custom panels in the settings editor.
#reason test/sidebar.test.ts Adds the command status bridge call to the sidebar fixture.
